 focus on  what we can add rather than take away so  if cheese is selling that you enjoy  enjoy it with other healthy fats in the  rotation and we're like very into our  farm fresh drinks because there's not  process at all farm fresh eggs are  supposed to be like amazing for you the  world of eggs is overwhelming as  it is so hard to know what's best from  an ethical and nutritional perspective  amidst the cage-free free-range organic  pasture-fed claims plastered across  every carton now for the most part these  terms have actual criteria that they  need to meet which is often a lot more  lenient than you might think but farm  fresh that's not a regulated term this  literally means nothing at all it's  basically just marketing because  ultimately all eggs come from some kind  of farm but assuming these eggs are  organic and pasture fed the consensus is  that organic eggs are slightly higher in  protein compared to conventional eggs  and there is some research suggesting  that pastured eggs are higher in vitamin  a e and omega-3s so if you can get that  two-for-one combo in an egg carton then  technically yes i guess you could say  they do have a nutritional edge and i  also always do love to support a good  local farmer i used to never be an  energy drink type of person like they  would make me feel jittery but now i am  fully into it like i fully love i love  it so while a celsius energy drink is  low in sugar it typically has about 200  milligrams of caffeine which is  equivalent to two cups of coffee so yeah  if you're sensitive to caffeine but you  want like a little boost of energy  pre-workout a half isn't a bad place to  start i know i cannot even handle any  caffeine afternoon but that's just me  [Music]  can we all find ourselves a partner who  feeds us mangoes like this no but really  for a post-workout snack mangoes are a  great fast-acting carb which will help  to replenish energy stores post-workout  and she did have about 15 grams of  protein pre-workout which is likely  within the four-hour anabolic window for  muscle protein synthesis and we've got  like another meal on the way so yeah  this little post-workout quickie snack  works for me okay i don't understand  people that purposely choose chicken  breasts unless you're like bodybuilding  counting every single calorie or  something like that if i buy chicken and  i open it and there's a ton of that i'm  like jackpot i do appreciate that for  once someone isn't scared of fat and i  agree a good chicken thigh is always  going to be superior to the breast in  the flavor department flavor town and  even for calorie counters i really don't  think this is a huge deal like a four  ounce portion of chicken thighs has only  50 calories more than a four ounce  serving of chicken breast so i think  that that's something most people could  easily work into their caloric budget  for the day i have an iron deficiency  okay so instead of taking iron pills  i'll like randomly eat salt from various  locations it's like an iron deficiency  thing it's like a quirk i don't know why  we do it so lauren is likely  experiencing something known as pica  which is an abnormal craving for a  non-food item which is often related to  nutrient deficiencies like iron however  pica cravings are not exclusive to salt  and can extend to really random textures  and taste like clay dirt or soap  [Applause]  and while craving a bit of extra salt is  benign compared to the other cases as  her partner said eating the salt doesn't  actually fix the issue so we would of  course want to prioritize treating the  underlying iron deficiency and that  means focusing on iron rich foods like  animal protein beans legumes nuts tofu  leafy greens fortified cereals and dark  chocolate and then pairing that with a  source of vitamin c so that could look  like a tofu stir-fry with bell peppers  like a lentil soup or bean chili with a  squeeze of lime on top or some dark  chocolate squares with some fruit as a